Map the signed-WORD tunnel color-vector aliases to the original image.

FUN_0042b720 calculates car lighting and shadow opacity on L2/L4. Ghidra
names the level-specific components sRam00465932/34/36 and 42/44/46;
they are overlapping words in scene_colour_vectors, not separate globals.
The port left all six as zero-initialized extern stubs. Original L2 loads
these components via current_level*8 + 0x465922/24/26 (WORD at 0x42ba89,
0x42ba9a,0x42baab; signed high-half DWORD at 0x42b9c4,0x42ba02,0x42ba2c).
These expressions access the same signed 16-bit image fields. L4 uses the
corresponding level-4 row. Preserve the original table reads through aliases.

Full read-only original L2 capture, cf454/ticks910: both images contain
4096 at 0x465932/34/36, but the port reads its host stubs as zero. Car 4's
color matrix should be 2626 per component, not zero; shadow opacity should
be 48, not 24. Positions, geometry, clocks, RNG and animation agree. The
result is a missing car shadow/incorrect body lighting at tunnel boundaries.

